course: dictionary
lesson: 15789
title: Unacquainted: not knowing or not having met
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unacquainted is a long word, but it has a clue inside. The start un- means not, and acquainted is about knowing something. So unacquainted means not knowing about something yet. «She was unacquainted with the rules of the game, so she asked her friends to explain them.» The clue is asked: she did not know the rules yet.
explain: The word can also mean that people have not met each other. «The two girls were unacquainted, so they stood apart at the party.» They had never been introduced, so they did not know each other. To check, swap in a simpler phrase such as didn't know or hadn't met. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Unacquainted is often used in stories and formal writing, and it usually comes with the phrase unacquainted with. In everyday talk people say didn't know or hadn't met. Keep the long word in your reading vocabulary, and use the simple words when you speak.
fact: Unacquainted is an adjective. It describes someone who is not familiar with something, or who has not met someone before.
fact: Unacquainted means not knowing about something, or not having met someone.
fact: The usual phrase is unacquainted with, as in «unacquainted with the town».
fact: The prefix un- means not, and acquainted means familiar, so unacquainted means not familiar.
fact: Simple swaps for unacquainted are didn't know and hadn't met.
exercise: «The new boy was unacquainted with the school rules.» What does unacquainted mean here? | *Did not know about the rules yet | Had broken every rule in the school | Liked the rules very much | Was angry with the teacher
exercise: «Mia and Sam were unacquainted before the trip.» What does unacquainted mean here? | Were shouting at each other | Were the same age | *Had not met before | Were best friends
exercise: «The visitor was unacquainted with our town.» Which simple phrase could replace unacquainted with? | Loved the town very much | Had lived there all her life | Was a famous town builder | *Did not know the town well
test: «Our guide was unacquainted with the cave, so she checked the map twice.» What does unacquainted mean? | Had explored the cave every day | Had painted the cave walls | Was afraid of the dark | *Did not know the cave well
test: Ravi says, «The two dogs were unacquainted, so they sniffed each other carefully.» What does unacquainted mean here? | Were very tired | *Had not met before | Were best friends for years | Were the same colour
exam: «The judges were unacquainted with the new game, so they asked the inventor to show them how to play.» What does unacquainted suggest? | They hated the game | They had invented it themselves | They had played it many times | *They did not know the game yet
